{"additions":7075,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #185\n\n## What\n\n- **`projects-filter \"<expression>\"`** (top-level) — a filter stacked on every view of the Projects page, saved or local: the view's filter, this one and the closed toggle are joined into one expression, so every term must hold. `(N filtered out)` counts everything hidden.\n- **`is:open` / `is:closed` / `is:merged`** — the board's GraphQL items query also reads the content's `state`; `ItemContent.state` (`#[serde(default)]`, disk-cache compatible) feeds `ProjectItem::state()`. A merged PR counts as closed as well as merged; an item without a known state (drafts, the CLI fallback path, older caches) counts as open. These were reported as unsupported before.\n- **`x`** — `BoardAction::ToggleClosed` hides closed issues and merged / closed PRs on top of whichever view is shown; the header says `· closed hidden`, a status message confirms. Survives refreshes and view switches. **`projects-hide-closed \"on\" | \"off\"`** (default `off`) sets the start state.\n\n## Docs / demo\n\nConfig Reference (en / ja: two new sections with CI-verified examples, table rows, unknown-block list, defaults dump), the Projects chapter (filter paragraph + key row + a paragraph on the stacked filters), README (en / ja), `assets/default.kdl` (`projects-hide-closed \"off\"`, a commented `projects-filter`, the `x` key). Fixtures re-recorded so the demo items carry `state` (7 of 8 are closed); the Projects demo presses `x` twice.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `state_terms_follow_the_content_state` (filter), the unsupported-token test now uses `is:archived`\n- `x_hides_closed_items_and_the_global_filter_stacks_on_the_view` (board pane)\n- `projects_filter_and_hide_closed_default_override_and_validation` (loader)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":51,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:49:47Z","deletions":3427,"headRefName":"feat/projects-hide-closed","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":188,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABM8CilA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nA few small but concrete issues remain (avoidable allocations in `ProjectItem::state()`, `projects-filter` returning `Some(\"\")` for empty expressions, and stale doc comments) that should be corrected before approval.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR enhances the Projects page by introducing a board-wide filter configuration and an `x` key toggle to hide closed/merged items, backed by fetching item `state` via the GraphQL path so `is:open|closed|merged` becomes locally evaluable. It also updates the default config, docs (EN/JA), demo tape/GIFs, and recorded fixtures to reflect the new behavior.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add top-level Projects config: `projects-filter \"<expression>\"` and `projects-hide-closed \"on\" | \"off\"`, and wire them into the Projects board pane.\n- Extend Projects items GraphQL query + types to capture `content.state`, enabling `is:open|closed|merged` filter terms and powering the closed-items toggle.\n- Update UI/header/status behavior, docs, demo tape/GIFs, and fixtures to demonstrate/verify the new filtering and toggle behavior.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `src/projects/state.rs` | Passes new config values into `BoardPane` initialization. |\r\n| `src/projects/panes/board.rs` | Implements global filter stacking and `x` toggle to hide closed/merged items; adds tests. |\r\n| `src/projects/domain/types.rs` | Adds `ItemContent.state` and `ProjectItem::state()` helper for filter/toggle logic. |\r\n| `src/projects/domain/graphql.rs` | Extends GraphQL query and JSON extraction to include `state` for Issue/PR content. |\r\n| `src/projects/domain/filter.rs` | Adds `is:open|closed|merged` parsing/evaluation using item state; updates tests/docs comment. |\r\n| `src/core/ui/status_bar.rs` | Adds `· closed hidden` marker in the Projects header when the toggle is active. |\r\n| `src/core/config/merge.rs` | Allows new top-level config nodes (`projects-filter`, `projects-hide-closed`) to merge/replace correctly. |\r\n| `src/core/config/loader.rs` | Parses/validates `projects-filter` and `projects-hide-closed`; adds loader tests. |\r\n| `assets/default.kdl` | Documents and adds defaults for new Projects config + binds `x` to `ToggleClosed`. |\r\n| `README.md` | Documents the new `x` behavior and how it relates to `projects-hide-closed` / `projects-filter`. |\r\n| `docs/README.ja.md` | Japanese README updates for the new `x` behavior and config knobs. |\r\n| `docs/guide/src/views-projects.md` | Explains stacked filters (view + `projects-filter` + closed toggle) and adds `x` key row. |\r\n| `docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md` | Japanese counterpart of Projects view doc updates (stacked filters + `x`). |\r\n| `docs/guide/src/config-reference.md` | Adds config reference sections for `projects-filter` and `projects-hide-closed`. |\r\n| `docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md` | Japanese counterpart config reference updates for the two new nodes. |\r\n| `tape/demo-projects.tape` | Demo now presses `x` twice to show hide/show closed items. |\r\n| `assets/demo-projects.gif` | Re-recorded Projects demo GIF reflecting the new `x` behavior. |\r\n| `assets/demo-github-issue.gif` | Re-recorded GIF (fixture/demo refresh alignment). |\r\n| `assets/demo-github-pr.gif` | Re-recorded GIF (fixture/demo refresh alignment). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-probe_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2.out` | Updated GraphQL probe fixture (rateLimit values changed). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-meta_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2.out` | Updated project meta fixture (rateLimit values changed). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-items_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2_-F_first_8.out` | Items fixture now includes `state` for Issue/PR content. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-pr-stacks_-F_owner_td72_-F_name_vig_-F_first_50.out` | Updated fixture output (rateLimit values changed). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/api_-i_repos_owner_repo_issues_state_all_sort_updated_direction_desc_per_page_1.out` | Updated REST change-check fixture (ETag/body content updated). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/issue_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_createdAt_parent_--limit_50.out` | Updated issue list fixture to include new issues 185–187. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/issue_view_185_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out` | New issue-view fixture for #185 (Projects filter + hide closed toggle). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/issue_view_186_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out` | New issue-view fixture for #186. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/issue_view_187_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out` | New issue-view fixture for #187. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_list_--limit_50_--json_databaseId_number_name_workflowName_status_conclusion_headBranch_event_createdAt_updatedAt_url.out` | Updated run list fixture to newer run history. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34440913700_--json_jobs.out` | New jobs JSON fixture for run 34440913700. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34440913700_--log_--job_102756580119.out` | New job log fixture for run 34440913700 / job 102756580119. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34440914114_--json_jobs.out` | New jobs JSON fixture for run 34440914114. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34441302809_--json_jobs.out` | New jobs JSON fixture for run 34441302809. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34441302809_--log_--job_102756730147.out` | New job log fixture for run 34441302809 / job 102756730147. |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747988_--json_jobs.out` | Removes an older jobs JSON fixture (cleanup/refresh). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747633_--json_jobs.out` | Removes an older jobs JSON fixture (cleanup/refresh). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747574_--json_jobs.out` | Removes an older jobs JSON fixture (cleanup/refresh). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747574_--log_--job_102388841140.out` | Removes an older job log fixture (cleanup/refresh). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747574_--log_--job_102388911539.out` | Removes an older job log fixture (cleanup/refresh). |\r\n| `tape/fixtures/issue_view_178_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out` | Removes an older issue-view fixture (fixture set refresh). |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 40/51 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-10T05:52:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"4f505425f1bcd3adb3ef2b08173c08c1f306d6a2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABM8EMVA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-10T05:57:03Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e90a0ffd6ccf15888aa9f3c7973e898282654616"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNP